      "writtenOn": "2022-08-11T18:37:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, the purpose of passing the handler is not dependency injection. Even though EthernetNetlinkMonitor has access to its parent class, the handler should be passed in as otherwise one may think to directly initialize mNetlinkMonitor where it\u0027s first declared (which will obviously be bad as mHandler is uninitialized at the time). Since sLog is a static final, I don\u0027t see a good reason to pass it in. It\u0027s always there anyways, and like Xiao says, it keeps the constructor simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "5879b78f_52282394",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 161,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 161,
